  <div class="boe-tab" data-tab="bandwidth" hidden>
    <div class="boe-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="boe-panel">
          <h3 class="boe-panel-title">Inputs</h3>
          <label class="boe-toggle">
            <input type="checkbox" id="bwLink" checked>
            <span class="boe-toggle-track"><span class="boe-toggle-thumb"></span></span>
            <span class="boe-toggle-label">Use peak RPS from Traffic</span>
          </label>
          <div class="boe-linked-note" id="bwLinkedNote">Currently <span id="bwLinkedValue">—</span> peak reads/sec and <span id="bwLinkedWriteValue">—</span> peak writes/sec, linked from Traffic.</div>
          <label class="boe-field" id="bwReadsField" hidden>
            <span class="boe-label">Peak read requests/sec<span class="boe-unit">RPS</span></span>
            <input class="boe-inp" type="number" min="0" step="any" id="bwReads" value="6000">
            <span class="boe-num-preview" id="bwReadsPreview"></span>
          </label>
          <label class="boe-field" id="bwWritesField" hidden>
            <span class="boe-label">Peak write requests/sec<span class="boe-unit">RPS</span></span>
            <input class="boe-inp" type="number" min="0" step="any" id="bwWrites" value="60">
            <span class="boe-num-preview" id="bwWritesPreview"></span>
          </label>
          <label class="boe-field">
            <span class="boe-label">Average response size<span class="boe-unit">B</span></span>
            <input class="boe-inp" type="number" min="0" step="any" id="respBytes" value="5120">
            <span class="boe-num-preview" id="respBytesPreview"></span>
            <span class="boe-hint">What actually goes out the wire: JSON payload, headers, TLS overhead. Usually bigger than the raw object.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="boe-field">
            <span class="boe-label">Average request size<span class="boe-unit">B</span></span>
            <input class="boe-inp" type="number" min="0" step="any" id="reqBytes" value="1024">
            <span class="boe-num-preview" id="reqBytesPreview"></span>
            <span class="boe-hint">Upload or write payload plus headers.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="boe-field">
            <span class="boe-label-row">
              <span class="boe-label-text">CDN / edge offload</span>
              <span class="boe-slide-val"><span id="cdnPctVal">60</span>%</span>
            </span>
            <input class="boe-range" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" id="cdnPct" value="60">
            <span class="boe-hint">Static assets and edge-cacheable responses that never reach your origin at all. This is a different lever from the Cache tab's hit ratio: caching saves your database, a CDN saves your network. 0% if you have no CDN.</span>
          </label>
          <label class="boe-field">
            <span class="boe-label">Protocol overhead<span class="boe-unit">: 1</span></span>
            <input class="boe-inp" type="number" min="1" step="any" id="bwOverhead" value="1.15">
            <span class="boe-hint">TCP/TLS handshakes, retries, and headers on top of the payload. 10–20% is typical.</span>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="boe-learn">
          <div class="boe-learn-label">Why it works</div>
          <p>Bandwidth has the same peak-vs-average split as everything else in this tool, but it shows up twice: the <strong>peak</strong> figure is what you provision, the link speed and NIC capacity that has to survive your busiest second. The <strong>monthly transfer</strong> figure is what you get billed for, built from average traffic over the whole month, not the peak.</p>
          <p>CDN offload and cache hit ratio look similar but solve different problems: caching keeps repeat reads off your database while still serving them from your own servers, so they still count as egress here. A CDN in front of that serves some of those reads from the edge instead, so they never touch your origin's network at all, that's the traffic this tab actually removes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="boe-panel">
          <h3 class="boe-panel-title">Peak bandwidth</h3>
          <div class="boe-out boe-out-big">
            <div class="boe-out-row"><span>Total, at peak</span><span class="boe-out-val" id="out-bwTotal">—</span></div>
            <div class="boe-formula">egress + ingress</div>
          </div>
          <div class="boe-out">
            <div class="boe-out-row"><span>Egress, reads out</span><span class="boe-out-val" id="out-bwEgress">—</span></div>
            <div class="boe-formula">origin read RPS × response size × overhead</div>
          </div>
          <div class="boe-out">
            <div class="boe-out-row"><span>Ingress, writes in</span><span class="boe-out-val" id="out-bwIngress">—</span></div>
            <div class="boe-formula">peak write RPS × request size × overhead</div>
          </div>
          <div class="boe-out">
            <div class="boe-out-row"><span>Origin read RPS after CDN</span><span class="boe-out-val" id="out-bwOriginRps">—<span class="boe-out-unit">RPS</span></span></div>
            <div class="boe-formula">peak read RPS × (1 − CDN offload)</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="boe-panel">
          <h3 class="boe-panel-title">Monthly transfer</h3>
          <div class="boe-out boe-out-big">
            <div class="boe-out-row"><span>Total per month</span><span class="boe-out-val" id="out-bwTotalMonth">—</span></div>
            <div class="boe-formula">average volume, not peak</div>
          </div>
          <div class="boe-out">
            <div class="boe-out-row"><span>Egress per month</span><span class="boe-out-val" id="out-bwEgressMonth">—</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="boe-out">
            <div class="boe-out-row"><span>Ingress per month</span><span class="boe-out-val" id="out-bwIngressMonth">—</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="boe-flag" id="flag-bandwidth-heavy">
          Multiple Gbps at peak is past what a single instance's NIC handles comfortably. Expect a load-balancer tier fanning out across several boxes, not one box with a bigger pipe.
        </div>
        <div class="boe-flag" id="flag-bandwidth-cost">
          At this monthly volume, egress pricing is likely a bigger line item than compute. A CDN, or a cloud provider with cheap/free egress, pays for itself here.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
